# 🔐 Python Password Vault

A secure command-line password manager built with Python that stores credentials inside an encrypted local vault.

The project demonstrates practical cybersecurity and secure software-development concepts including **Argon2id password-based key derivation, AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption, cryptographically secure random generation, secure file permissions, password rotation, tamper detection, and automated security testing**.

---

## 📌 Overview

Python Password Vault is a local CLI password manager where users can securely store and retrieve credentials using a single master password.

The master password is **never stored inside the vault**.

Instead, it is combined with a randomly generated salt and processed using **Argon2id** to derive a 256-bit encryption key.

That key is then used with **AES-256-GCM** to encrypt and authenticate the vault contents.

### High-Level Security Flow

```text
                 Master Password
                        │
                        ▼
                  Random Salt
                        │
                        ▼
                    Argon2id
                        │
                        ▼
                 256-bit Key
                        │
                        ▼
                 AES-256-GCM
                        │
                        ▼
               Encrypted Vault
                  vault.json

